{% comment %}
  The reassurance that belongs next to the money: who dispatches this, when it
  goes out, whether you can collect it, and that a pharmacist is reachable
  before you buy.

  It lived in the footer only, which is the one place a shopper deciding whether
  to click Add to bag is not looking.

  Every line here is either always true or driven by real data. Two in
  particular are deliberately NOT free text:

    Dispatch cutoff renders only when settings.dispatch_cutoff is filled in.
    Blank by default, so an unconfirmed time never appears beside a buy button.
    Note that 12 collection FAQ answers still say "before 3pm" independently —
    see setup/MAINTENANCE.md before setting this.

    Click & Collect renders only from variant.store_availabilities, which
    Shopify populates from the locations where local pickup is actually
    enabled. If pickup is not configured, nothing renders. The theme therefore
    cannot promise collection the store has not switched on, and the store
    count is Shopify's, not ours.

  The pharmacy lines (PSI-registered, Ask a pharmacist, and the PSI logo) show
  when the product is a medicine — tagged with the restricted tag, or its type
  starts with "Pharmacy", which is how the client's catalogue types every
  Medicines & Health product — or when the Product section's checkbox turns
  them on for everything. On a vitamin they are noise; on a pharmacy-only
  medicine they are the point. The footer's PSI logo is the regulatory one and
  stays on every page regardless; this copy is reassurance, not compliance.
  With no product passed (the cart) the lines always show: a bag is mixed.

  Accepts:
    variant       — optional; pickup lines need it, so pass it on a product page
    product       — optional; gates the pharmacy lines as above
    all_products  — true to show the pharmacy lines on every product
    compact       — true for the cart's smaller type
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign type_size = '15px'
  assign line_gap = '11px'
  if compact
    assign type_size = '13.5px'
    assign line_gap = '11px'
  endif

  assign pharmacy = true
  if product and all_products != true
    assign pharmacy = false
    capture restricted
      render 'product-restricted', product: product
    endcapture
    assign type_prefix = product.type | downcase | slice: 0, 8
    if restricted == 'true' or type_prefix == 'pharmacy'
      assign pharmacy = true
    endif
  endif

  assign pickup_locations = ''
  if variant and variant.store_availabilities
    assign pickup_locations = variant.store_availabilities | where: 'available'
  endif
-%}

<div data-buy-assurance style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:{{ line_gap }};">

  {%- if settings.dispatch_cutoff != blank -%}
    <div style="display:flex; gap:10px; align-items:flex-start; font-size:{{ type_size }}; line-height:1.6; color:{% if compact %}#666b60{% else %}#3a3d39{% endif %};">
      <span style="color:var(--c-accent); font-weight:800;">&check;</span>
      <span>Order before <strong style="font-weight:800;">{{ settings.dispatch_cutoff }}</strong> {{ settings.dispatch_days | default: 'Monday to Friday' }} for same-day dispatch</span>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if pickup_locations != blank and pickup_locations.size > 0 -%}
    <div style="display:flex; gap:10px; align-items:flex-start; font-size:{{ type_size }}; line-height:1.6; color:{% if compact %}#666b60{% else %}#3a3d39{% endif %};">
      <span style="color:var(--c-accent); font-weight:800;">&check;</span>
      <span>
        <strong style="font-weight:800;">Click &amp; Collect</strong> from
        {% if pickup_locations.size == 1 %}{{ pickup_locations.first.location.name }}{% else %}{{ pickup_locations.size }} of our stores{% endif %}
        &mdash; <a href="/pages/click-and-collect" class="hov-green-dk" style="color:var(--c-dark); font-weight:700; text-decoration:underline; text-underline-offset:3px;">how it works</a>
      </span>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if pharmacy -%}
  <div style="display:flex; gap:10px; align-items:flex-start; font-size:{{ type_size }}; line-height:1.6; color:{% if compact %}#666b60{% else %}#3a3d39{% endif %};">
    <span style="color:var(--c-accent); font-weight:800;">&check;</span>
    <span>Dispatched from our <a href="/pages/internet-supply-pharmacy" class="hov-green-dk" style="color:var(--c-dark); font-weight:700; text-decoration:underline; text-underline-offset:3px;">PSI-registered</a> Irish pharmacy</span>
  </div>

  <div style="display:flex; gap:10px; align-items:flex-start; font-size:{{ type_size }}; line-height:1.6; color:{% if compact %}#666b60{% else %}#3a3d39{% endif %};">
    <span style="color:var(--c-accent); font-weight:800;">&check;</span>
    <span><a href="/pages/contact-us" class="hov-green-dk" style="color:var(--c-dark); font-weight:700; text-decoration:underline; text-underline-offset:3px;">Ask a pharmacist</a> before you buy &mdash; in store, by phone or by email</span>
  </div>

  {%- unless compact -%}
    {%- comment -%} The PSI mark carries more weight than the words beside it, so the
        product page shows it. The cart already has the shopper's commitment and
        does not need the extra weight. {%- endcomment -%}
    <a href="https://registrations.thepsi.ie/search-isl/?search=10001884" rel="noopener" style="display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:10px; margin-top:2px; width:fit-content;">
      <img src="{{ 'psi-logo.avif' | asset_url }}" alt="PSI registered internet supply pharmacy" width="86" height="72" loading="lazy" style="height:72px; width:auto; display:block; border-radius:4px;">
      <span style="font-size:12.5px; line-height:1.45; color:#666b60; max-width:22ch;">Verify this pharmacy on the PSI register</span>
    </a>
  {%- endunless -%}
  {%- endif -%}

</div>
